From 12b587f6cedbb7d166a8482b85f4c62ee4598b83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment <experiment@invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:08:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: let the firmware select the rate of ordinary
 data frames

Every frame was sent with the descriptor's fixed-rate bit and OFDM
6 Mbit/s, which caps the air time at about 2.9 Mbit/s of goodput whatever
the link quality. Clear the fixed-rate bit for ordinary data only, so the
firmware's rate selection runs over the station record's rate set that
mac80211 supplied at association; the descriptor's rate field remains as
its fallback. Management and security frames keep their fixed 6 Mbit/s
descriptors, and the TX-done event's rate field, already parsed and
logged, becomes the measurement. One variable for one boot.

Internal experiment archive; synthetic non-certifying author,
not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h
index f4dcc5268..5c94e011f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h
@@ -158,7 +158,12 @@ mt6797_join_tx_data_descriptor(const unsigned char *frame, size_t bytes,
 	d[6] = 0x80; /* Protected frame, TID 0, no header padding. */
 	d[7] = 1U << 2; /* Own-MAC 1. */
 	d[10] = lifetime;
-	d[11] = 0x80; /* Fixed rate enabled, zero power offset. */
+	/* Fixed rate disabled, zero power offset: ordinary data uses the
+	 * firmware's rate selection over the station record's rate set. The
+	 * rate field below is then the firmware's fallback only; management
+	 * and security frames keep their fixed OFDM 6 Mbps descriptors.
+	 */
+	d[11] = 0;
 	d[12] = count; d[13] = count >> 8;
 	d[20] = pid; d[21] = 2; /* TX status to MCU. */
 	d[26] = (0x4bU << 2) & 255; d[27] = (0x4bU << 2) >> 8;
